    <h2>What makes Level 29 tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Three moves load the motorcycle before anything moves it: the cycling old man at step 1, the old man in the wheelchair at step 2, a rocket at step 4. The grandma's helmet at step 3 goes the other way, onto the Grim Reaper. A run reads that as filling the bike and stalls, because a loaded bike is not a fuelled one. Step 10 taps the fuel tank, step 11 pours the engine oil in, and the bike only has fuel after those two moves. Tapping an empty tank looks like a wasted move and it is not.</p>
    <p>Two of the twelve moves are aimed at the pursuer rather than at the bike: the helmet at step 3 and the grandma's bag at step 8. Both leave the getaway and land on the Grim Reaper, so this is not purely a level about outrunning him. The lipstick is a single item used twice, on the old man in hospital clothes at step 6 and then on the old man in a leather jacket at step 7, and the grandma's backpack is tapped at step 5, between the rocket load and the first lipstick move, and nothing else in the level opens it.</p>
    <p>The moon appears twice and both moves are unusual. Step 9 drags the moon onto the motorcycle mirror, which is a small target on a bike you have just finished loading. Step 12 swipes down on the same moon, one gesture instead of a drop, and it is the last move of the level. The level is a chase, and the moon is the only object in it that belongs to neither side. If the bike is loaded and still sitting there, the answer is the tank rather than another passenger. The checklist below tracks the two taps, the two gifts to Death and the two moon moves.</p>

    <h2>Two taps, two gifts, two moons<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The bike fills up quickly; these are the moves that actually end the chase:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The load, steps 1, 2 and 4. Cycling old man, wheelchair old man, rocket, all onto the motorcycle.</li>
      <li>The helmet, step 3. It goes to the Grim Reaper, not onto the bike with the other three.</li>
      <li>The backpack, step 5. Tapped between the rocket and the first lipstick move; it is the only container in the level.</li>
      <li>The lipstick, steps 6 and 7. One item, two old men: hospital clothes first, leather jacket second.</li>
      <li>The grandma's bag, step 8. The second move that hands something to the Grim Reaper.</li>
      <li>The fuel tank, steps 10 and 11. Tap it, then pour the engine oil in. The tank comes before the oil.</li>
      <li>The moon, steps 9 and 12. Dragged onto the mirror, then swiped down as the final move.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Full bike, full tank, moon in the mirror: the three things that have to be true before the swipe at 12.</p>

